<Quota name="Q-PerUser" type="calendar">
  <DisplayName>Tier 3: one user, within their department, within this calling app, per day</DisplayName>
  <!--
    RE-KEYED and RE-GRANULARISED 2026-09-17. Was "Identifier ref
    request.header.x-colt-user-oid", TimeUnit minute, reading
    req_per_min_per_user — a flat per-minute rate check, shared across
    whichever app happened to call this proxy. Replaced with the innermost
    tier of the nested daily hierarchy, keyed on mcp_dept_user_key
    ("{client_id}:{department}:{oid}", built by AM-QuotaKeys.xml) so it is
    generalised the same way Q-PerDepartment above is: a second MCP-calling
    use case partitions automatically, no edit needed here.

    Identifier is a raw request header pair, not a verified JWT claim —
    there is no user token on this hop (see docs/24 section 3.2). Only as
    trustworthy as naas-agent-api's own code, the same "asserted, not
    proven" trust level docs/23 section 4.3 already accepts for department
    on the browser-facing proxy.
  -->
  <StartTime>2026-01-01 00:00:00</StartTime>
  <Interval>1</Interval>
  <TimeUnit>day</TimeUnit>
  <Allow count="2000" countRef="verifyapikey.VA-ApiKey.apiproduct.req_per_day_per_user"/>
  <Identifier ref="mcp_dept_user_key"/>
  <Distributed>true</Distributed>
  <Synchronous>true</Synchronous>
</Quota>
